{title: The Decree of Darius}
{subtitle: Ezra 4:24; 5:5–8; 6:1–5; 6:6–12; 6:13–15; Haggai 1:1–4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
So the work on the house of [Eb]God in Jerusalem came to a [Bb]halt
It stood still until the second year [Eb]of the reign of Darius king of [Bb]Persia
The eye of their God was on the el[Eb]ders of the Jews
They were [Gm]not stopped until a [F]report could go to [Eb]Darius
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Let the house be rebuilt as a place [Eb]for offering sacrifices
Let [Bb]its foundations be laid with sixty cu[Eb]bits of height and width
The [Gm]cost is to be [F]paid from the [Eb]royal treasury
I, [Bb]Darius, have [F]issued [Eb]this decree
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Then King [Bb]Darius issued an or[Eb]der and a search was made
In the [Bb]archives where the treasures were stored [Eb]in Babylon
At Ecba[Gm]tana in the [F]fortress in [Eb]Media a scroll was found
King [Bb]Cyrus issued this or[F]der in his [Eb]first year
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Keep far away from there [Eb]Tattenai [Bb]and Shet-har-bo-ze-nai
Leave [Eb]the work on this house of God alone
[Gm]Let the governor of [F]the Jews and the el[Eb]ders rebuild this house
The [Bb]cost is to be paid [F]in full from the [Eb]royal treasury
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
This [Bb]house was completed on the third day [Eb]of the month of Adar
In [Bb]the sixth year of [F]the reign of [Eb]King Darius
{end_of_verse}
